section: ghci
synopsis: ``evalStmt <expr>`` break flags apply only to the main expression thread
issues: #28080 #26064
mrs: !16922

description: {
  The per-thread debugger flags (single-step, step-out and break-on-exception)
  are now set only on the sandbox thread forked to evaluate a new expression,
  rather than globally on all threads.

  As a consequence, ``:step <expr>``, where ``<expr>`` forks a thread, now stops
  at the next breakpoint in the thread evaluating ``<expr>``, not at a
  breakpoint in any forked thread. A forked thread may still stop at a
  breakpoint that was explicitly enabled, and ``:step``-ing from there enables
  stepping for that thread.
}
